<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 265 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 265 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 265 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.2 BLN    1.2 BLN    1.25 BLN   =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    650 MLN    950 MLN    1.215 BLN  =</p>
<p> DETAILS</p>
<p> BILLS/FRG TO NOV 18  650 MLN!   =	    =	    =</p>
<p> BAND 1  BANK BILLS		  300 MLN*   265 MLN*</p>
<p>! INTEREST RATE 5-31/32 PERCENT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE 5-15/16 PERCENT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
